{
  "skip": false,
  "summary": "Fixes the stated UX issue: when the profile website's domain matches (or is a parent of) the instance domain, the full URL path is now shown instead of just the bare host. The core same-host and 3-part-subdomain cases are correct and covered by tests. One gap in the domain-relationship logic below is worth fixing before merge; domain comparisons are also case-sensitive (`example.com` vs `EXAMPLE.com` won't match), which is a smaller follow-up worth a mention.",
  "event": "COMMENT",
  "findings": [
    {
      "path": "app/serializers/user_serializer.rb",
      "line": 149,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "severity": "Important",
      "title": "Parent/subdomain check only works in one direction",
      "body": "This only handles the case where `discourse_host` is a subdomain of `website_host` (e.g. discourse_host=`forums.example.com`, website=`example.com`, tested in the spec). The mirror case — instance at the bare domain (`example.com`) and website at a subdomain of it (`blog.example.com`) — falls through to the `else` branch's own final expression and returns just `website_host` without the path, even though it's clearly the same site family. Since the same-domain checks above are meant to be symmetric (same registrable domain = show full path), this asymmetry silently drops the path for a plausible real-world configuration."
    }
  ]
}
